# Code owners (task #198, QCH-S11). GitHub requires a review from the listed
# owner before a pull request touching these paths can merge — a supply-chain
# control so no change to consensus, crypto, execution, or the deploy tooling
# lands without the maintainer's explicit approval.
#
# Replace `@owner` with the real GitHub handle(s) of the maintainer(s). Enforcement
# also needs branch protection on the default branch with "Require review from
# Code Owners" enabled (repo Settings → Branches).

# Default: everything is owned by the maintainer.
*                       @owner

# Security-critical subsystems — consensus, crypto, the execution/ledger boundary,
# and the STARK light-client. A change here should get extra scrutiny.
/crates/qchain-consensus/    @owner
/crates/qchain-crypto/       @owner
/crates/qchain-execution/    @owner
/crates/qchain-stark/        @owner
/crates/qchain-node/         @owner

# Supply-chain surfaces: the lockfile, the pinned toolchain, CI, the Dockerfile,
# and the deploy tooling that runs on real hosts.
/Cargo.lock             @owner
/rust-toolchain.toml    @owner
/.github/               @owner
/Dockerfile             @owner
/deploy/                @owner
